---
// v3-G (2026-10-08): a homepage card's direct links — where you get the product (directLinks in
// pages/index.astro) — as one quiet row right under the card. It sits OUTSIDE the card's <a>: a
// link can't contain a link, and the card's own hover (veil lift, zoom, title colour) stays as is.
// 2026-10-09 (user: the row under the card "排版不搭" — put them next to the title): the row is
// absolutely positioned inside the card's wrapper (index.astro gives it `relative group`) so it
// sits on the title's line — small card: right end of the title row; large card: bottom-right of
// the image, level with the title on the bottom-left. Still OUTSIDE the card's <a> in the DOM (a
// link can't hold a link); the wrapper's `group` keeps the card's hover (zoom, veil) on while the
// pointer is on a button. Entrance: the row fades in only after its card has finished rising
// (global.css transition-delay), so the two never sit misaligned mid-reveal, and it never moves.
// 2026-10-09 (user: button and title had no hierarchy — dim the buttons): mist text, a faint
// white/10 border, semibold; they brighten to paper on hover. The title stays the brightest thing.
// Earlier the same day (user: "看起来不像按钮"): small pills in the hero's secondary-button language —
// rounded-full, border-line, paper text, accent border/text on hover — one size down (px-4 py-2,
// text-xs) so they read as buttons without competing with the hero's accent button. Nothing here
// moves: the row fades in with its card's reveal, opacity only (global.css .card-links; AGENTS.md:
// a link that moves between mousedown and mouseup loses the click). py-2 = a taller hit area for
// the trailing custom cursor; with mt-1 the link text box starts 12 px below the card's bottom edge
// (a small card's title row, the large card's image). The large card passes px-5: its title is
// inset 20 px on the image, and the row lines up under it. The explicit {' '} before the arrow: inside this
// nested map Astro drops the plain space (it rendered "Adobe Exchange↗"). No links → nothing.
interface Props {
  links: { label: string; url: string }[];
  // true = the large card: the buttons sit on the image's bottom-right, level with the title
  // that sits on its bottom-left. false = a small card: right end of the title row under the image.
  overlay?: boolean;
}
const { links, overlay = false } = Astro.props;
---

{
  links.length > 0 && (
    <p class:list={[
      'card-links z-20 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2',
      // small cards on phones: a title + two pills don't fit one line (Cubby), so below sm the row
      // flows under the title; from sm up it sits at the title row's right end.
      overlay ? 'absolute bottom-7 right-5 justify-end md:bottom-[30px]' : 'mt-3 sm:absolute sm:bottom-0 sm:right-0 sm:mt-0 sm:justify-end',
    ]}>
      {links.map((l) => (
        <a href={l.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-cursor="Open" class:list={[
          'inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap rounded-full border border-white/10 px-4 py-2 font-display text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-mist transition-colors hover:border-white/40 hover:text-paper',
          overlay && 'bg-ink/40 backdrop-blur-sm',
        ]}>
          {l.label}{' '}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </p>
  )
}
